/T (38 .\(a\) If the reverberation time of a hall is long, then the multiple echoes will interfere with the original sound. For this reason, nothing will be heard distinctly. So, the reverberation time of the hall should be very short. \(b\) A sound is heard only if the body vibrates with a frequency more than 20 Hz and less than 20,000 Hz. The pendulum oscillates with a frequency less than 20 Hz. Hence, no sound is heard. \(c\) This is due to the quality of timbre of sound waves.)
